{
  "cues": [
    {
      "start_seconds": 0.12,
      "end_seconds": 2.26,
      "text": "How could a clock tell\nsailors where they"
    },
    {
      "start_seconds": 2.321,
      "end_seconds": 3.141,
      "text": "were in the ocean?"
    },
    {
      "start_seconds": 4.081,
      "end_seconds": 6.861,
      "text": "In the 1700s,\nships far from land"
    },
    {
      "start_seconds": 7.042,
      "end_seconds": 9.662,
      "text": "struggled to work out how\nfar east or west"
    },
    {
      "start_seconds": 9.722,
      "end_seconds": 10.442,
      "text": "they had sailed."
    },
    {
      "start_seconds": 11.022,
      "end_seconds": 12.443,
      "text": "One answer was time."
    },
    {
      "start_seconds": 12.923,
      "end_seconds": 14.443,
      "text": "When the sun\nreached its highest"
    },
    {
      "start_seconds": 14.543,
      "end_seconds": 17.024,
      "text": "point, sailors knew\nit was noon on the ship."
    },
    {
      "start_seconds": 17.484,
      "end_seconds": 19.584,
      "text": "If a clock still showed\nthe time back home,"
    },
    {
      "start_seconds": 19.844,
      "end_seconds": 21.705,
      "text": "they could compare\nthe two and calculate"
    },
    {
      "start_seconds": 21.745,
      "end_seconds": 23.365,
      "text": "their position east or west."
    },
    {
      "start_seconds": 23.845,
      "end_seconds": 26.366,
      "text": "But a clock had to stay\naccurate through a long,"
    },
    {
      "start_seconds": 26.546,
      "end_seconds": 27.446,
      "text": "rolling voyage."
    },
    {
      "start_seconds": 27.946,
      "end_seconds": 30.767,
      "text": "English clockmaker\nJohn Harrison spent years"
    },
    {
      "start_seconds": 30.847,
      "end_seconds": 32.027,
      "text": "working on one that could."
    },
    {
      "start_seconds": 32.507,
      "end_seconds": 35.808,
      "text": "In 1761, his son took\nHarrison's watch,"
    },
    {
      "start_seconds": 36.068,
      "end_seconds": 38.728,
      "text": "known as H4,\non a voyage to Jamaica."
    },
    {
      "start_seconds": 39.169,
      "end_seconds": 40.749,
      "text": "It kept time\naccurately enough"
    },
    {
      "start_seconds": 40.829,
      "end_seconds": 42.889,
      "text": "to prove that the method\ncould work at sea."
    },
    {
      "start_seconds": 43.329,
      "end_seconds": 45.65,
      "text": "The ship could use the time\nback home to help"
    },
    {
      "start_seconds": 45.71,
      "end_seconds": 47.01,
      "text": "find its place on the ocean."
    }
  ]
}